{"t": "2026-09-25T23:52:52+0530", "event": "operator_note", "text": "Operator stop of the first baseline_ctrl launch (23:33-23:36): its 4 DataLoader workers grew ~1.7 GB private per 30 s each and the machine reached 98.6 % RAM; the OS killed a worker at 23:33:32 (event above). Reproduced in isolation: training-config loader, 1 worker, +1.25 GB per 10 batches (one batch retained per batch); dataset alone in one process: flat. Fix: b_pipeline/stacked_dataset.py::aerotrack_collate stacks into shared memory inside workers (bit-exact vs the old stack; 4 workers flat at ~1.7 GB over 60 batches). A loader-memory probe was added to the pre-flight; the grid was relaunched with the same command at 23:44 and baseline_ctrl restarted from scratch (no epoch had finished)."}
{"t": "2026-09-25T23:53:01+0530", "event": "operator_note", "text": "The pre-flight at 23:24:46 (ok: False) failed only its 'no other GPU job' check: on Windows the venv python.exe is a launcher whose child is the real interpreter, and the check flagged the runner's own launcher (its parent) as a foreign job. Fixed in run_grid.py (ancestors count as the runner's own tree) before any training; the next pre-flight passed every check."}
{"t": "2026-09-26T01:56:15+0530", "event": "operator_note", "text": "The runner started at 23:44:35 (pid 16996) was killed externally between 01:50:50 and 01:51:52 (no traceback, no event; its console log simply stops). Its training child kept running and finished baseline_ctrl cleanly at 01:53:32 (20/20 epochs, rc 0, recorded by train_ablation.py). Most likely the agent tool that launched the runner cleaned up the process it had started. Mitigations: --detach now starts the runner through a short-lived spawner (never a process of the calling shell), and a relaunched runner first waits for any still-running step of an earlier runner (orphan adoption). Relaunched with the same command; baseline_ctrl is verified from its files, not retrained."}
